title image: harden place_paint witness, close REDS #85
prompt Autonomous loop -- reds-first: a recurring lantern found this turn (apostrophe closing a witness grep) booked and closed before opening new feature work.
think The place_paint lap hit the apostrophe-in-witness red -- the printed GREEN line carried "source's", and the witness grep guard wraps output in single quotes, so the apostrophe closed the shell string. I first reworded apostrophe-free to land the lap. Reds-first then asked: this lantern has now fired on conic_paint AND place_paint this turn alone -- a lantern that fires twice becomes a loom.
think Reading crux/REDS.md, the loom ALREADY EXISTS: REDS #76 (HUNK49) taught the convention -- check witness claims with Rishi's native `assert out contains "..."`, never `printf ... | grep` over interpolated output, because native contains never routes through a shell. The fix was real yet local: it converted the two HUNK witnesses but never reached the image-family witness template, so every new image witness (compose_tiled, conic_paint, place_paint) copied the fragile printf-grep forward.
think The disciplined close: convert place_paint_witness.rish to native contains, and RESTORE the natural apostrophe in the module GREEN line to prove on metal the check no longer breaks -- exactly as REDS #76 restored its apostrophe. Verified GREEN with the apostrophe present.
obs Booked REDS #85 with all three fields (what went wrong, what caught it, what it taught: a loom only guards the code that actually adopts its convention). The wider sweep of the remaining printf-grep image witnesses (compose_tiled, conic_paint, kin) to native contains is booked as its own next round rather than widened here -- narrow scope, one keystone per round.
obs Shipped as its own signed increment (send often), separate from the place_paint feature round, so the reds closure is followable on GitHub on its own commit.
loom witness=place_paint_witness check=native_contains green_with_apostrophe=proven reds=85_closed
file tools/place_paint_witness.rish GREEN claim now checked with native `assert selftest.out contains` -- shell-proof
file image/place_paint.rye GREEN line apostrophe restored to prove the check is robust
file crux/REDS.md row 85 books the REDS #76 -> #85 recurrence and its close
file crux/REMEMBER.md Git nib refreshed to the reds-closing commit
recommend keep-going next agent-doable open-media rung, and (booked) sweep the remaining image witnesses to native contains; no custody gate reached.
